        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "This “rule” dates from the middle of the twentieth century. It has no basis in logic or grammar, as the allegedly incorrect use of hopefully parallels the usage of other words that no one complains about, words such as candidly, frankly, sadly, and happily:",
